# Session Log

Cross-machine continuity log for Claude Code sessions on this project.
This file is tracked in git so it can be synced between laptops (commit + push / pull).

Newest entries at the top. Each entry: date, machine (optional), summary of
what was done, decisions made, and what's next.

---

## 2026-09-25 (later still)
- Embedded the resolved QoS into each published payload in
  `ZenohJavaTlsPub.java` (e.g. `hello #1 from pure-Java (mTLS)
  [qos=DEFAULT (no ext)]`), so a subscriber sees what QoS a message
  was sent with, not just the publisher's console banner. Reused the
  same `qosLabel` string for both the banner and the payload.
  Verified with `mvn -q package`.
- Updated README's mTLS publisher section to mention this.
- Committed and pushed all outstanding work from this session
  (--topic flag + QoS-in-payload + doc updates).

## 2026-09-25 (later)
- Added `--topic=<keyExpr>` support to `runTlsPub.bat`, plus a batch-level
  `TOPIC` default (`996dfb6c880346559dff117458d27b66/zenoh-client/test-topic`).
- Rewrote the arg-handling in `runTlsPub.bat`: replaced the old
  `:no_args`/`:one_arg`/`:two_args`/`:three_or_more_args` positional
  dispatch with a two-pass parser (a non-destructive scan for
  `--topic=`, then a shift-loop that fills keyExpr/count/interval or
  just count/interval when `--topic` is present). This was necessary
  because `--topic` can appear anywhere in the args and must not be
  forwarded to the Java sample (it has no `--topic` flag of its own).
  Precedence: `--topic` flag > positional keyExpr > `TOPIC` default.
  Verified by hand-tracing the parser logic (couldn't exec cmd.exe
  directly from this sandboxed Bash tool to test interactively).
- Updated README.md's "mTLS publisher with QoS" section and the
  in-file REM/help text to document the new flag and precedence rule.
- Not yet committed/pushed — waiting on user confirmation.

## 2026-09-25
- Added project-level and global (`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`) notes: how to
  reauthenticate with Google (`gcloud auth login` +
  `gcloud auth application-default login`), and a documentation style
  rule (no em-dashes, write in simple, clear, complete sentences).
